VERDICT: ALL FIXED - zero open findings.

Close-out documentation reviews (2026-10-26, post-round-77)
----------------------------------------------------------
After the evidence refresh at c7e4ec3, two independent reviewers re-read
the close-out files: DeepSeek V4.1 Flash (Copilot BYOK, xhigh) and Meta
Muse Spark 1.3 Contributor (local BYOK proxy, xhigh). Together they
reported 12 documentation-precision issues (9 and 3, two of them shared),
listed here as the ten distinct defects. None touched product code:

- the evidence README named 1fdeaf5 as the capture tree for gates.log,
  which its own header places at 1b5ce29;
- the research-battery capture date was wrong (2026-10-22 capture,
  2026-10-23 commit, not 2026-10-24);
- two historical ci.log blocks still said "HEAD" and "in_progress" for
  runs whose final conclusions are known (cancelled/superseded);
- review-final.log was labelled as unchanged since 1b5ce29 although its
  header was corrected later (verdicts unchanged);
- the evidence README repeated "Step 6" for the agent-kit row;
- the round-73/75/76 commit attribution in review-final.log was too
  broad (round-73 fixes landed at e06df6d, the round-75 bound at
  625f22c, the round-76 sweep at f6efd0d);
- the reasoning-effort scope read differently in two files;
- an orphaned C ABI/WASM paragraph read as part of round 77;
- the external tooling-proposal path looked repo-relative;
- deterministic artifacts that reproduce byte-for-byte need a provenance
  record, because a re-run leaves no git trace.

All were fixed. conformance/evidence/REFRESH.md now records the re-run at
1fdeaf5 with a SHA-256 pin per unchanged artifact, the README gives the
true capture tree per row, ci.log records final conclusions only, and the
commit attribution and effort scope are stated once and consistently.
Neither reviewer found a contradiction in the round counts, test counts,
run verdicts, vector/tool counts, or the review verdicts themselves.

VERDICT: all documentation findings fixed.

Full-diff review through the local meta-muse proxy (goal section 8.6)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
The goal requires the fresh full-diff review via the Copilot CLI against
the local meta-muse-spark-1.3-contributor proxy at `--reasoning-effort
xhigh`, with zero open findings and the log captured. Five passes ran
over the complete goal diff: `c5366f4` (26 findings), `2721e98` (3),
`0cde3fa` (4), `39daa44` (3), and `ebc8ca0` (2). Every real finding was
fixed at the cause with a regression test; three were rejected with a
documented contract.

Fixed across the passes:
- mixed `Int`/`Float` subtraction and division were missing, although
  spec section 3.3 says mixed arithmetic promotes (T001 instead);
- `Float` and mixed `Int`/`Float` ordering fell through to T001 entirely;
  the new `cmp_int_float` compares exactly beyond 2^53;
- the `DurationMs` ratio cast and blob sizes could wrap negative;
- float equality used an epsilon window instead of structural equality;
- `spec/conformance.md` said 16 cases and claimed the manifest predated
  Blob and mode (it has 21 cases, 19 differential);
- `bindings/go/SPEC.md` carried a wrong full hash for the pinned module;
- the CycloneDX SBOMs missed `blake3` and `base64`;
- workflows lacked job timeouts, read permissions, and pipefail in the
  piped verification steps;
- `codegen_equivalence.py` reported PASS when the zod install failed;
- evidence logs, counts, and capture headers had drifted.

Rejected with evidence: the FFI budget struct documents "every other zero
selects its shipped default" (`docs/FFI.md`, `active-ffi/active.h`); the
prompt result label 1.1.0 is a historical run label (`prompts/README.md`);
and `--budget-profile` is a real `check`/`eval` flag.

The full transcripts are in `conformance/evidence/review-muse-fulldiff.log`.
